---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// PHOTOGRAPHY HUB
//
// Added Aug 2026. Photography was scattered across five pages: portraits buried
// on /weddings, real estate on its own page, headshots mentioned on /business,
// corporate portraits in /portfolio, and seniors standing alone. Somebody
// looking for a photographer had nowhere to land.
//
// This is a PARENT page, not a replacement. /real-estate-photography and
// /senior-portraits keep their own URLs and their own ranking history (never
// rename a published slug) and are linked from here. The nav swapped those two
// entries for this one, so the section grew while the nav got shorter.
//
// Family session frames moved here from the Portraits block on /weddings, which
// is now weddings only.
//
// PRICING confirmed by Geoff 2026-08-07: immediate family $600, extended $850.
// Carried over from the retired Pixieset site and re-confirmed. Senior and real
// estate numbers live on their own pages; this table mirrors them, so if one
// changes, change both.
//
// HEADSHOTS: mentioned in copy, deliberately no gallery. The only real headshot
// frames are from CBSR's July 16 day and have not been cleared for publication
// (Geoff's call, Aug 2026). Do NOT add a headshot gallery using the corporate
// portraits as a stand-in: they are a different thing and it would read as
// padding. Add one when there are cleared headshots.
---
<Layout
  title="Nashville Photography | SDub Media"
  description="Photography around Nashville: family sessions from $600, senior portraits $750, real estate listings, headshots and corporate work. Full-resolution galleries, no proof-print upsell."
>
<section>
  <div class="container-narrow text-center">
    <span class="eyebrow">Photography</span>
    <h1>A photographer for the shoot,<br />not whoever is free that day.</h1>
    <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; margin-top: 1.5rem;">Listings, seniors, families, headshots. Our photographers each shoot one thing constantly, which is why a listing comes back in 48 hours and nobody is learning your kind of shoot on your afternoon.</p>
    <div style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Book a session</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="container" style="margin-top: 3.5rem;">
    <img class="wedding-hero-img" src="/images/portraits/family-desert-path.jpg"
         alt="A family of four on a desert path at golden hour, the parents dancing while their two children lean against fence posts"
         width="1600" height="1069" />
  </div>
</section>

<section style="background: var(--soft);">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">What we shoot</span>
      <h2>Four kinds of work, and someone who shoots each one constantly.</h2>
    </div>
    {/* Site tile pattern, two-up so four cards fill both rows. Two of these
        have their own page and carry an arrow; family and headshots do not
        have one yet, so they are plain tiles rather than links to nowhere. */}
    <div class="tiles tiles--two">
      <a href="/real-estate-photography" class="tile" style="color: inherit;">
        <img class="tile-image" src="/images/real-estate/kitchen-island.jpg" alt="A bright kitchen with a large island, photographed for a listing" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="1069" />
        <h3>Real Estate</h3>
        <p>Listings, interiors and aerials, priced per listing and turned around fast enough to matter. It has its own page because agents book it differently to everything else.</p>
        <span class="door-arrow">Real estate photography &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/senior-portraits" class="tile" style="color: inherit;">
        <img class="tile-image" src="/images/seniors/cap-toss-path.jpg" alt="A graduate in a gold gown throwing her cap on a hedge lined path" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="1069" />
        <h3>Senior Portraits</h3>
        <p>Cap and gown plus whatever they actually want to be seen in, shot on location rather than against a studio wall. $750 for the session.</p>
        <span class="door-arrow">Senior portraits &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <div class="tile">
        <img class="tile-image" src="/images/portraits/family-desert-seated.jpg" alt="A family of four seated together at golden hour among Joshua trees" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="1069" />
        <h3>Family Sessions</h3>
        <p>Including the extended-family version, for the one week a year everybody is finally in the same state. Shot outdoors, on location. $600, or $850 with the extended family.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/business" class="tile" style="color: inherit;">
        <img class="tile-image" src="/images/corporate/team-portrait.jpg" alt="A full brokerage team photographed together on steps outdoors" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="1067" />
        <h3>Headshots and Corporate</h3>
        <p>On site at your office, so nobody loses half a day to it. We run headshot days for a brokerage, rotating through their offices one at a time, and they usually ride along with a video crew that is already there.</p>
        <span class="door-arrow">Business photography &rarr;</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Recent work</span>
      <h2>Real sessions, real clients.</h2>
    </div>
    {/* Filenames here were renamed Aug 2026 to match what the files actually
        contain. Three of them described photos that were not in them at all
        ("portrait-with-dogs" is a family of four in the desert, "family-baby-kiss"
        is a couple), and the wrong alt text had been live on /weddings for
        months. If an image is ever swapped, rename the file and rewrite the alt
        in the same commit.

        Deliberately mixed rather than grouped: the point of this page is range,
        and the child pages already show depth in one subject. Client frames are
        published anonymously, filenames describe the frame and never the
        client, and EXIF is stripped on save. */}
    <div class="photo-strip-tall">
      <img src="/images/seniors/portrait-smiling.jpg" alt="A high school senior in a white dress leaning against a column" loading="lazy" width="1069" height="1600" />
      <img src="/images/portraits/grandparents-grandkids.jpg" alt="Grandparents surrounded by six grandchildren in a winter field" loading="lazy" width="1069" height="1600" />
      <img src="/images/corporate/portrait-trio.jpg" alt="Three colleagues photographed together outdoors" loading="lazy" width="1100" height="1650" />
      <img src="/images/seniors/cap-raised.jpg" alt="A graduate holding her cap overhead, backlit by late sun" loading="lazy" width="1069" height="1600" />
    </div>
    <div class="wedding-strip" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
      <img src="/images/portraits/couple-autumn-lane.jpg" alt="A couple photographed together on a lane in full autumn colour" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="1069" />
      <img src="/images/real-estate/great-room.jpg" alt="A bright great room photographed for a listing" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="1069" />
      <img src="/images/portraits/family-desert-seated.jpg" alt="A family of four seated together at golden hour among Joshua trees" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="1069" />
      <img src="/images/corporate/team-portrait.jpg" alt="A full brokerage team photographed together on steps outdoors" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="1067" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="background: var(--soft);">
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Who shoots it</span>
      <h2>Specialists, not one person with a camera.</h2>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size: 1.1rem;">Most small production companies are one generalist who books help when the calendar gets tight. We are built the other way.</p>
    {/* Roles only, never names or faces: the team is not willing to appear on
        the marketing site and that is their call. Same rule as /about, where
        these roles are confirmed. Do not pad this list. */}
    <ul class="facts" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
      <li>A photographer who shoots <strong>homes only</strong>, which is why listings come back in 48 hours</li>
      <li>A photographer who covers <strong>live events</strong>, where you get one attempt at every moment</li>
      <li>The <strong>owner</strong>, who shoots portraits, families and seniors, and has done every job the company sells</li>
      <li><strong>Editing in house</strong>, so your gallery never sits in someone else's queue</li>
    </ul>
    <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">More on <a href="/about">who shows up</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">What you get</span>
      <h2>The files, at full resolution, without an upsell.</h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="facts">
      <li><strong>A private online gallery</strong>, shared by link. Download the whole set or pick individual frames</li>
      <li><strong>Full-resolution files</strong>. No proof prints, no per-file charges, no watermarks on work you paid for</li>
      <li><strong>Portrait sessions keep the untouched originals</strong>, EXIF and colour profile intact, for the shoots where the file itself is the product</li>
      <li><strong>Sized for where it is going</strong>, so a listing photo and a social crop are not the same download</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="background: var(--soft);">
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">What it costs</span>
      <h2>Published where we can, quoted where it depends.</h2>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size: 1.1rem;">Some of this prices cleanly and some genuinely depends on the job. Where it prices cleanly, the number is on the page.</p>
    <div style="margin-top: 2rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden;">
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding: 1.15rem 1.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);">
        <span><strong>Senior session</strong><br><span style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted);">Outfit changes, cap and gown, family frames, full gallery</span></span>
        <span style="white-space: nowrap;"><strong>$750</strong></span>
      </div>
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding: 1.15rem 1.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);">
        <span><strong>Real estate</strong><br><span style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted);">Priced per listing, by size</span></span>
        <span style="white-space: nowrap;"><a href="/real-estate-photography">See pricing</a></span>
      </div>
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding: 1.15rem 1.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);">
        <span><strong>Immediate family</strong><br><span style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted);">A guided session and a curated set of edited files in your gallery</span></span>
        <span style="white-space: nowrap;"><strong>$600</strong></span>
      </div>
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding: 1.15rem 1.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);">
        <span><strong>Extended family</strong><br><span style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted);">Group portraits plus the natural ones, for when everybody is finally together</span></span>
        <span style="white-space: nowrap;"><strong>$850</strong></span>
      </div>
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding: 1.15rem 1.25rem;">
        <span><strong>Headshots and corporate</strong><br><span style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted);">Per person on a headshot day, or per shoot</span></span>
        <span style="white-space: nowrap;">Per day</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">Ask and we will send numbers the same day. If you already have a video shoot booked, say so: adding stills to a day we are already on site for costs less than booking it separately.</p>
    <div style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Get a quote</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</Layout>
